    "answer": {
      "short": "$2$",
      "worked": "There are $42$ scores, split into two halves of $21$ scores each.\n\nThe lower quartile is the median of the first $21$ scores: the 11th score overall. Scores in positions 10–16 are $3$, so $Q_1=3$.\n\nThe upper quartile is the median of the second half: its 11th score, or the 32nd score overall. Scores in positions 21–34 are $5$, so $Q_3=5$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{IQR}&=Q_3-Q_1\\\\\\mathrm{IQR}&=5-3\\\\\\mathrm{IQR}&=2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
